+# Document Management API
+
+Express + TypeScript API for users, hierarchical folders, documents, granular
+sharing and an activity log. All state lives in memory and resets on restart.
+
+```ts
+import { createApp } from './src/app.js'; // also re-exported from ./src/index.ts
+const app = createApp(); // fresh, isolated store per call
+app.listen(3000);
+```
+
+```bash
+npm run build && npm run lint && npm test
+npx tsx src/index.ts          # run the server (PORT env var, default 3000)
+```
+
+## Permission model
+
+Roles, least to most permissive: `viewer` → `editor` → `owner`.
+
+| Action | Required role |
+| --- | --- |
+| read a folder/document | `viewer` |
+| update, create a child folder/document | `editor` |
+| share (grant `viewer`/`editor`) | `editor` |
+| delete, grant/change `owner`, revoke a share | `owner` |
+
+- The creator of a resource is recorded as its owner and cannot be demoted or removed.
+- Permissions are **inherited down the folder tree**: a role on a folder applies to
+  every nested folder and document.
+- When access arrives through several paths (direct share + one or more ancestor
+  folders) the **most permissive** role wins.
+
+## Routes
+
+All routes except register/login require `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
+
+### Auth & users
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| POST | `/auth/register`, `/register`, `/users` | `{username, password}` → 201 `{id, username, token}` |
+| POST | `/auth/login`, `/login` | → 200 `{token, user}` |
+| POST | `/auth/logout` | 204, invalidates the token |
+| GET | `/auth/me`, `/me`, `/users/me` | current user |
+| GET | `/users`, `/users/:id` | user directory (id + username) |
+
+### Folders
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| POST | `/folders` | `{name, parentId?}` — needs `editor` on the parent |
+| GET | `/folders` | readable folders; `?parentId=` filter |
+| GET | `/folders/:id` | folder + visible `children` and `documents` |
+| GET | `/folders/:id/children`, `/folders/:id/documents` | |
+| PATCH/PUT | `/folders/:id` | rename / move (cycles rejected with 400) |
+| DELETE | `/folders/:id` | 204, cascades to nested folders and documents |
+
+### Documents
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| POST | `/documents` | `{title, content?, folderId}` |
+| POST | `/folders/:folderId/documents` | same, folder from the path |
+| GET | `/documents` | readable documents; `?folderId=` filter |
+| GET | `/documents/:id` | |
+| PATCH/PUT | `/documents/:id` | `{title?, content?, folderId?}` |
+| DELETE | `/documents/:id` | 204 |
+
+### Sharing
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| POST | `/documents/:id/share`, `/folders/:id/share` | `{userId \| username, role}` → 201 |
+| POST | `/share` | `{resourceType, resourceId, userId, role}` |
+| PUT | `/{documents\|folders}/:id/share/:userId` | change a role |
+| GET | `/{documents\|folders}/:id/shares` (`/permissions`) | direct + inherited access list |
+| DELETE | `/{documents\|folders}/:id/share/:userId` | 204 |
+
+### Activity
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| GET | `/activity` (`/activities`) | oldest → newest; filters: `resourceType`, `resourceId`, `action`, `userId`, `limit` |
+
+Logged actions: `folder.create|update|delete`, `document.create|update|delete`,
+`share.grant`, `share.revoke`. Each entry has `{id, action, userId, resourceType,
+resourceId, details?, timestamp}`. Callers only see entries they performed or that
+target a resource they can currently read.
+
+## Status codes
+
+`200` ok · `201` created · `204` deleted/logged out · `400` validation · `401`
+missing/invalid token · `403` authenticated but insufficient role · `404` unknown
+resource or user · `409` username taken.
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+src/
+  app.ts           createApp() — wiring, aliases, error handling
+  index.ts         re-exports + standalone server entry point
+  store.ts         in-memory Maps, password hashing, token issuing, activity log
+  permissions.ts   effective-role resolution and require* guards
+  sharing.ts       grant/revoke rules and access lists
+  auth.ts          credential validation + bearer-token middleware
+  routes/          auth, folders, documents, shares, activity routers
+tests/             supertest suites (auth, folders, documents, permissions, activity)
+```
